name w4-01-floor
timeout 420
time 1999-03-24T10:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W4, SORTIE 1 OF 10 - ALLIED FORCE 1999: MOUNTAINS, CLOUD, AND AN AIR DEFENCE THAT WILL NOT EMIT.
# THE 15,000 FT FLOOR, PRICED IN BOTH CURRENCIES.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w4-allied-force.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none - it IS the control, of BOTH w4-02-overcast.fbm (one `wx` line) and
# w4-03-below-floor.fbm (one fact: the ingress altitude).
#
# THE ANCHOR: NATO flew Allied Force under a hard altitude floor of 15,000 ft or higher, forced by
# heavy MANPADS and AAA [T3]. 15,000 ft = 4,572.0 m [DERIVED, 0.3048 m/ft], and that number is the
# spawn and every waypoint altitude in this file. W4's spec says the floor "is declared in every
# striker's `wp` altitudes and is the thing the missions push against"; this sortie is where it is
# PRICED, because its own §Gaps says that without a short-range threat the floor is "an arbitrary
# altitude". `C1` closed on 2026-07-28 and the floor now has its cause standing under it.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WHAT DOES THE FLOOR COST THE BOMB, AND WHAT DOES IT BUY AGAINST THE
# LAYER THAT CAUSED IT? Two numbers, both out of this file: `stores DELIVERY aimErrM`, and the pair
# `zone_flak_s` / `zone_sambelt_s` beside the short-range positions' own `site` lines.
#
# THE ARENA, and every coordinate in it is [SET] inside the anchor's Kosovo engagement zone
# (~42.2-43.2 N, 20.2-21.8 E [T4, approximate]). Ingress west->east along 42.70 N, which is the
# direction the packages came from. Scale: 1 deg of latitude = 111,320 m, 1 deg of longitude at
# 42.70 N = 111,320 * cos(42.70) = 81,833 m [DERIVED].
#   `k1tgt` target_soft      42.70000 21.10000 - a dispersed vehicle park, the archetype (W4 Knowledge 2:
#                            no specific target list was sourced, and none is invented)
#   `k1man` 9K32 Strela-2M   42.70000 21.06000, 3.3 km short of the aim point, 2 rounds. Ceiling 2,300 m
#   `k1flk` ZU-23-2          42.70000 21.09000, on the target, 40 rounds. Ceiling 1,500 m
#   `k1sam` 2K12 Kub         42.66000 20.98000, 3 rounds, `emcon free`. Ceiling 7,000 m, 6-22 km
# The two `zone` cylinders are the floor written down as geometry (`C23`): `flak` 0-3,500 m and
# `sambelt` 3,500-8,000 m, both 14 km around 42.70/20.98. The band edge is [SET] at 3,500 m because
# that is the highest MANPADS ceiling in the catalogue (9K38 Igla) - i.e. the top of the layer the
# anchor names as the floor's cause, not a round number.
#
# THE FOUR STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES OF THIS CAMPAIGN, repeated in all ten files because a reader who
# skips them reads every result backwards:
#   1. THERE IS NO TERRAIN MASKING (gap C4), AND W4 IS ITS ACCEPTANCE TEST. The anchor's own phrase
#      for the Yugoslav method is "concealment under weather and mountainous terrain". A mountain
#      that breaks no line of sight is this campaign's central shortfall: every detection below is a
#      detection over a flat, transparent world, so every range at which something is found here is an
#      UPPER BOUND on what the real geometry would have given, and every "the position saw it" is a
#      statement about the catalogue's range gate and nothing else.
#   2. THE GROUND IS A 0 m PLANE. Flown under `--elev const`. The real Kosovo under this arena is
#      546-1,193 m (MEASURED off `fb-tiles` /elev at 42.70/21.10 = 546.34 m, 42.60/20.90 = 586.42 m,
#      42.70/20.70 = 588.60 m, 43.00/21.00 = 1,192.75 m), so a "4,572 m" ingress here is 4,572 m over
#      a plane and about 3,980 m over the real ridge line. The campaign file says why the campaign is
#      not flown on tiles.
#   3. CLOUD REACHES ONLY THE EYE (gap C16). Cloud data gets to `FBWorld::SetWeather` and to
#      `sensors/FBVisualSystem`'s transmittance march, and to nothing else - not the radar, not the
#      release, not the fuze. Sortie 02 is where that is measured rather than asserted.
#   4. `FBMissionRunner` ends the WHOLE run at the first flight-monitor K.O. (`FirstFlightKo`), so
#      every engagement in a W4 file with two of them is laid out on that clock.
#
# WHICH LAYER THIS FILE MEASURES: the SHORT-RANGE one, and it measures it by being out of its reach.
# There is no fighter in 01, 02 or 03.
#
# READING RULE (binding): exit 0 is the pass and it is NOT the answer. Read, in this order:
# (1) `stores DELIVERY aimErrM` against attack-ccrp.fbm's own low-level number on the same ground,
# (2) `zone_flak_s` and `zone_sambelt_s` on the striker's telemetry, (3) how many `site TRACK` and
# `site LAUNCH` lines `k1man` and `k1flk` produced, and (4) how many rounds `k1sam` fired and how many
# arrived. Do NOT read "the striker survived" as a defensive failure - read WHY.
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint bc669334ab3c0186, exit 0): THE FLOOR COSTS 2.4 m OF PREDICTION ERROR PER
# KILOMETRE OF ALTITUDE AND BUYS THE ENTIRE SHORT-RANGE LAYER.
#   the bomb          `stores DELIVERY ... predErrM=58.05 aimErrM=41.09 aimLongM=36.80 aimAcrossM=18.28`
#                     at t=183.1. `k1tgt` DESTROYED - 41.09 m is inside an Mk-82's ~45 m fragment
#                     radius, and that margin is what the floor spends. THE CLEAN QUANTITY IS THE
#                     COMPUTER'S OWN ERROR, `predErrM`, because the delivered error is quantised by the
#                     release tick; measured on a threat-free ladder over this arena (attribution A2b),
#                     48.62 m at 600 m / 49.27 at 900 / 49.91 at 1,200 / 51.51 at 2,000 / 53.69 at
#                     3,000 / **58.08 at 4,572** / 63.45 at 6,000, i.e. **+2.38 m per 1,000 m**
#                     [DERIVED from the ladder] and +19.4 % from 600 m to the floor. The lateral half
#                     scales with the throw and is monotone throughout: `aimAcrossM` 8.33 m at 600 m
#                     against 21.68 m at 6,000 m. W4's spec quotes 22.2 m for `attack-ccrp.fbm` as the
#                     low-level reference; that figure is superseded by the frame round of 2026-07-29
#                     and the same mission re-measured under this binary with `--elev const` gives
#                     **30.89 m** - but it is a DIFFERENT arena, and the ladder above is the control
#                     that actually answers the spec's question
#   the short layer   `k1man` (Strela-2M) and `k1flk` (ZU-23-2): **0 `site TRACK`, 0 `site LAUNCH`.**
#                     The gun's own eye DOES see the jet - `site CUE unit=k1flk brgDeg=3.40
#                     signal=0.773` at t=110.3 - and it never engages, because 4,572 m is above its
#                     1,500 m ceiling. THE FLOOR IS NOT A DETERRENT, IT IS AN ENVELOPE WALL, and the
#                     cue line is the proof that the wall is the envelope and not a blind sensor
#   the zones         `zone_flak_s` = **0.0 s**, `zone_sambelt_s` = **285.2 s** (t=72.9-224.9 and
#                     t=260.9-394.1). `objective avoid zone flak exposure 0` MET
#   the SAM layer     `k1sam` tracks at t=42.7 from 21.9 km and fires **3 of 3** 3M9 at t=69.5 / 96.4 /
#                     123.3 - and not one arrives
#   THE DEFECT THIS SORTIE FOUND, and it is not in the subsystem the sortie was written about. At the
#   third launch the position goes `site STATE ... from=ENGAGE to=RELOAD why="rails empty"` (2K12
#   `RailCount` 3, `ReloadS` 600), Reload radiates beam 0 ONLY, and 0.2 s later all three rounds log
#   `missile ILLUMINATION_LOST`. Round 2 was **1,776.6 m from the aircraft with 27.1 s of flight behind
#   it** - about 9.6 s from arrival at its 185 m/s closure. ATTRIBUTED WITH A CONTROL RUN (rule 4,
#   attribution A4): the identical file with `set rounds 4`, so the MAGAZINE is not empty, loses the
#   illumination at the IDENTICAL tick t=123.5 with identical `tofS`/`rangeM` on all three rounds. IT
#   IS THE RAILS, NOT THE MAGAZINE: a semi-active battery that starts a reload throws away every round
#   it has in the air, and a 2K12's effective magazine against one target is therefore 2 and not 3.
#   Reported, not fixed, and not tuned around.

zone flak 42.70000 20.98000 14000 0 3500
zone sambelt 42.70000 20.98000 14000 3500 8000

unit k1str
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 42.70000 20.60000 4572 90.0 450     # 40.9 km west of the aim point, AT the anchor's floor
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off                          # a single striker on a briefed steerpoint radiates nothing
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 42.70000 21.10000 4572 450             # THE AIM POINT: the active steerpoint IS the target
  wp 42.70000 20.70000 4572 450             # egress, flown after the break turn
  objective kill unit k1tgt
  objective survive
  objective avoid zone flak

unit k1man
  module sa7
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.06000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 2

unit k1flk
  module zu23
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.09000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 40

unit k1sam
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 42.66000 20.98000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 3

unit k1tgt
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.10000 ground 90.0 0
